                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">               
                            <locus from="1" to="20"/>
                            <title ref="LIT1467GadlaI"/>
                            <note>According to a note by <persName ref="PRS3182ContiRo"/> (cf. <ref target="#e1"/>), the text was copied 
                                from a manuscript of ‘Ḥayq’, which refers probably to the monastery <placeName ref="INS0327DHE"/>.
                                The manuscript was used by Stanislas Kur in his edition <bibl><ptr target="bm:Kur1965IyasusMoa"/></bibl>
                                with the siglum ‘B’. Some parts of the text have been published and translated by Carlo Conti Rossini, as well:
                                <bibl><ptr target="bm:ContiRossini1922Zague"/></bibl>. An unpublished Italian translation is attested in 
                                manuscript Conti Rossini 121 in the same collection in the Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei. <!-- Add ms ref -->
                                The manuscript consists of two quires, which are not in the correct order. The text starts on <locus target="#11r"/>.
                                The second half of the text is placed in front on <locus from="1" to="10"/>.
                                Wrongly attributed ‘KRZ 82’ in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/>
                                    <citedRange unit="page">221</citedRange></bibl>, which is infact  ‘KRZ 86’ (= Kinefe-Rigb Zelleke 86).</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                        </msItem>
